Both upstreams are MIT licensed. Their full license texts are reproduced in
LICENSES-THIRD-PARTY.md — kept out of LICENSE so that GitHub's license detector
sees a single unambiguous MIT and labels the repository correctly.

What was changed: each upstream ships an installer, a CLI, a statusline, slash
commands, a mode-tracker state file, intensity levels and a benchmark suite. The
persona prose is the only part that changes model behavior, so only that was
kept — level-filtered to a single baked-in intensity, with the self-referential
mode names ("caveman", "ponytail") replaced by the axis they implement. This
extraction pattern is taken from a private agent-runtime codebase, which did the
same reduction in order to inject the two personas into a Claude Agent SDK
worker. The measurements behind this project's headline numbers come from that
system; the report is republished, with the operator's identifiers removed, in
docs/BENCHMARK.md.

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

personas/01-detail-less.md is original to this work. It has no upstream — it
began as a local Claude Code SessionStart hook and its few-shot examples were
genericized for publication.
